---SCREEN
=LINLIB/visi preferences setup

  use arrow keys or .:TA... then .:NL... or .:SP... to make menu choice 

  the profile that was found first will fix the compiled default settings:
    personal:    $VHSET/$TERM		
    system-wide: /etc/vhset/$TERM	

  do the following to create personal profile:

    export VHSET=~/.vhset ; 
    mkdir -p $VHSET ; 
    touch $VHSET/$TERM

  Please,
  refer to 'man vhset' for full explanation of this program
  
=
There is one hidden page called with .'0 key. It allows to change
keypad activation key and labels for arrow keys which usually are never changed.
---END
